riscos-mesa: Mesa's EGL demos in desktop windows
================================================

Five of the EGL demos from mesa-demos 9.0.0, built from their unchanged
source. mesa-demos' small window library (eglut) was given a RISC OS back
end, so each demo gets a Wimp window through riscos-mesa's native EGL (the
window handle is the EGL native window). They multitask like any other
desktop program.

Needs SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport (the !Run files load them from
System:Modules if they aren't loaded already).

!EGLGears   the classic gears, desktop OpenGL 1.x
!ES1Gears   the same gears in OpenGL ES 1.1
!ES2Gears   the gears drawn with OpenGL ES 2.0 shaders
!ES1Torus   a textured torus in OpenGL ES 1.1 (Space pauses, T changes
            the texture format)
!EGLTri     a shaded triangle, desktop OpenGL; it only redraws when you
            press a key (as on Linux)

Cursor keys rotate the view. Escape or the close icon quits. Click in the
window first so it has the input focus. The window can be resized.

The demos print their frame rate every 5 seconds (the gears) or other
information. It goes to the file Output inside each application, and the
newest line is shown in the window's title bar.

Please report the frame rates in the title bars, and anything that looks
wrong.

Sources and the porting guide: docs/porting/mesa-demos.md in the
riscos-mesa repository. Licence: MIT (see each application's Licence file).
